## What to deliver

Build and rig the fortress up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a tiered, prowed armored citadel raised on legs,
carrying a big main turret and forward cannon, a side-mounted turret out on each flank,
and a sweeping radar vane. **Author the three required animations** as F-curves with
the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands: `march` (a walk whose feet plant flat and
still, then lift and swing — with weight, not a weightless slide), `bombardment` (the
guns working while the fortress stands its ground), and the self-playing `radar_spin`.
The animations are the fixed contract — produce all three, by those names; the parts
and joints that realize them are yours. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded
per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
